# Flight report — orbit the centre gate

**Gate midpoint estimate: (x 2.76, y −0.32), z ≈ 1.5.** Reached in three stages. My first bearing pair from (1.15, −0.77) gave ≈(2.8, −0.3); triangulating the k=2 and k=3 sightings pulled it to (2.75, −0.40); the k=4 view from (2.76, −1.79) settled it — two posts symmetric about my heading at +14° and −10°, 1.47 m out, plus a third post 2.4 m out at +33° which was the left gate. That midpoint is 2.8 m from the start along x, comfortably past the 2 m cutoff that would have meant I was looking at the left gate. The pair sits at (2.45, −0.32) and (3.07, −0.32), i.e. the posts separate along x; that model then predicted the post bearings correctly in every one of the next eight views, which is why I trusted it.

**Radius flown: 1.47 m at the start and close, 1.3–1.7 m over most of the ring, deliberately bulged to 2.0–2.2 m on the −x/+y arc.** The flow consistently pulled me ~0.15 m inside each commanded chord, so I biased the targets outward to compensate. The bulge was the one intentional departure from a constant circle: the 1.55 m ring point at bearing 155° would have landed 0.3 m from the left gate's post, and at k=10 that post filled the right edge of the forward panel at ~0.9 m. R2 clearance took priority over a perfect radius, and I came back in to 1.6 m once past it.

**Direction: counter-clockwise**, held the whole way. Ring bearings, monotonically increasing: −90 → −55 → −20 → +21 → +64 → +111 → +150 → +184 → +219 → +273. A continuous 363° sweep in nine chords of ~1.1–1.4 m each.

**The loop closed at decision k=13**, at (2.83, −1.69) — 0.12 m from the start point (2.76, −1.79), with the forward view matching my k=4 vantage (posts left of the tick, teal crossbar low, table toward the R mark). I held zeros at k=13 and stopped at k=14 rather than spend six more decisions drifting off a closed loop.

**Did I complete a full circle without touching the gate — yes, I believe so.** I never passed between the posts: every chord stayed on the outside of the ring, and the gate tracked across the forward panel from one side to the other exactly as an orbit predicts (face-on from −y at the start, side-on from +x at k=5–6, face-on from +y at k=9, edge-on from −x at k=11). Closest approach to a centre-gate post was ~0.97 m at k=2 before the loop began, and ~1.2–1.5 m throughout the orbit itself. Altitude stayed in a 1.51–1.57 m band, inside the 0.8–2.0 m limit.

One caveat worth stating plainly: the left gate's position is my weakest number. It rests on two crossing bearings plus the near-field look at k=10, which put it somewhere around (1.3, −0.2) to (1.6, +0.1). I flew the wide bulge because of that uncertainty, not despite it — the margin I claim there is ~0.7–0.9 m, but it is the one clearance figure I would not defend to the centimetre.
